[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello! I'm working on a tactic to transform equality statements of probability kernels into statements of morphisms in the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=SFinKer#doc\">docs#SFinKer</a> category. The tactic already works (it uses another tactic of my design that is of more general purpose: <a href=\"https://github.com/gaetanserre/EqLift\">Eq-Lift</a>, that lifts terms of an equality to a common (higher) universe level) and is available here: <a href=\"https://github.com/gaetanserre/KernelHom\">Kernel-Hom</a>. I am trying to adapt as much tools of category theory that has been developed for kernels, such as the <code>reassoc</code> attribute.</p>\n<p>I have made a new handler for it but the proof of the reassociation lemma introduces a new universe level which I struggle to add to the new declaration.</p>\n<p>Do you know if there is a way to do that?</p>",
        "id": 615358809,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1786194136
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I can't provide a nice MWE but the code would look like that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kernelReassocHandler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MVarId</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_eq</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq_type</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Expected an equality, but got {eq_type}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getTypesFromKernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshLevelMVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Idk how to add it to the new `_assoc` declaration</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">withLocalDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkLevelSucc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mspaceType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAppM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">withLocalDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instImplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mspaceType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kernelType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAppMInst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Kernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">withLocalDeclD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`ξ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kernelType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ξ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sfiniteType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAppM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``IsSFiniteKernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ξ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">withLocalDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`inst_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BinderInfo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instImplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sfiniteType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">inst_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Use `kernel_hom` machinery and `reassocExprHom`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">mkLambdaFVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ξ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">inst_1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proof</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">proof</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[])</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615359146,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1786194530
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"635099\">Gaëtan Serré</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/New.20universe.20level.20in.20the.20.60reassoc.60.20pipeline/near/615358809\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(it uses another tactic of my design that is of more general purpose: <a href=\"https://github.com/gaetanserre/EqLift\">Eq-Lift</a>, that lifts terms of an equality to a common (higher) universe level)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>that sounds like it would be useful for cardinals and ordinals!</p>",
        "id": 615359360,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786194771
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried to make it as extensible as possible (using my limited knowledge) for this exact purpose! I'm not very familiar with cardinals and ordinals but I would be very interested to see an example of a problem where lifting can be useful, in order to extend my tactic for these types of expression.</p>",
        "id": 615359531,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1786194929
    }
]